      "type": "thinking",
      "thinking": "I lean toward yes, batching makes sense: land branches after targeted tests plus a compile check, then run the full suite roughly every two hours against master's tip. If that batch goes red, bisect among the merges in that window and revert the offender, while only deploying from a verified green tip. The trade-off is master could stay red for up to two hours, but it saves significant compute since each full gate run eats 15\u201325 minutes across 32 cores\u2014worth it, especially factoring in perf tests too.\n\nSince this is really their call on workflow, I'll give my recommendation clearly and go ahead and adopt it rather than just leaving it open-ended, then keep things brief and move on.\n\n",
      "thinkingSignature": ""
    },
